\\\"body\\\": \\\"The sleep and anesthesia discussion keeps the theory from being purely anatomical. A thalamocortical system can have the right wiring, but if its dynamics collapse into undifferentiated or bistable responses, integrated information should drop. That seems especially relevant for non-reporting patients, where behavior alone may be a poor guide.\\\",\n            \\\"parent_ref\\\": None,\n            \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n                \\\"score\\\": 25,\n                \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Strongly ties source claims about state-dependent dynamics to the practical assessment problem.\\\"\n            }\n        }\n    ]\n}\nprint(json.dumps(obj, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(\\\",\\\", \\\":\\\")))\nPY\n\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
